# low-lying electronic states of air species
# format: species-ID N  temp1 relax1 degen1 spin1 dof1  ... tempN relaxN degenN spinN dofN
#   temp = state energy / kB (K), relax = inverse relaxation collision number,
#   degen = total state degeneracy, spin = spin degeneracy class, dof = unused
# level data: NIST atomic/molecular spectra (fine-structure levels grouped)
#
# these ladders set the electronic partition functions used to derive
# detailed-balance reverse reaction rates; the ground-state degeneracies
# alone change the equilibrium constant of N2 + O <-> NO + N by ~1.8x
N2 3   0.0 0.01 1 1 0   72231.4 0.01 3 3 0   85778.0 0.01 6 3 0
O  3   0.0 0.01 9 3 0   22830.0 0.01 5 1 0   48620.0 0.01 1 1 0
N  3   0.0 0.01 4 4 0   27660.0 0.01 10 2 0  41490.0 0.01 6 2 0
NO 2   0.0 0.01 4 2 0   63200.0 0.01 2 2 0
